/*  EXPECTED: REJECTED at type-check, identically by both backends.
    An object made in a rabbit has its field replaced by a series from outside; a rabbit's series
    is then inserted into that field.

    The field is judged by what it now is, which outlives the rabbit (docs/SOUNDNESS.md, obligation O2). */

Define object bag with (the series of series of number items).
Define outer as a series of series of number.
Pull a rabbit.
    Define b as a new bag { the items a series of series of number }.
    b's items becomes outer.
    Define inner as a series of number with (1, 2, 3).
    Insert inner into b's items.
Done.
State the number of outer.
